The City of Valdosta and Lowndes County do hereby establish a Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) Policy Committee to ensure a continuing, cooperative, and comprehensive transportation planning process for the Valdosta/Lowndes MPO and that said policy committee be empowered to establish a technical coordinating committee, a citizens advisory committee and other ad hoc or advisory committees as required or deemed necessary. The MPO policy committee will:
(1) Be the forum for cooperative decision-making and shall consist of principal elected officials of the participating local general governments within the Valdosta/Lowndes County MPO area and appointed officials of designated agencies, which oversee or operate major transportation modes within the area. The MPO policy committee:
a. Reviews and approves all transportation study programs;
b. Ensures that the transportation program is current and responsive to laws, rules, regulations;
c. Designates and prioritizes transportation improvement projects recommended in the planning process;
d. Serves as liaison between the planning process and the governmental units and designates membership and operations of the technical coordinating committee, the citizens advisory committee and other ad hoc study committees.
(2) Consist of the following members:
a. Chairman, Lowndes County Board of Commissioners (or representative);
b. Mayor, City of Valdosta (or representative);
c. Annually rotating small city mayor (mayor or representative of Hahira, Lake Park, Remerton or Dasher);
d. Lowndes County Manager;
e. Valdosta Manager;
f. SGRDC executive director;
g. Georgia DOT Commissioner (or representative);
h. Nonvoting members:
1. Division administrator—Federal Highway Administration;
2. Regional administrator—Federal Transit Administration.
(Res. No. 2003-16, 11-20-2003)

